<title>NETHERLANDS: EU disagrees over Albania force.</title>
<headline>EU disagrees over Albania force.</headline>
<dateline>APELDOORN, Netherlands 1997-03-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union foreign ministers failed to agree on Saturday on whether to provide military assistance to Albania, Spanish Foreign Minister Abel Matutes said.</p>
<p>Matutes told reporters that Italy, Greece, Denmark and France had been in favour of military intervention of some sort to restore order in Albania.</p>
<p>But he said Britain, Germany and Sweden had been vehemently opposed to such action. &quot;The majority is against,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>Diplomats said the ministers had discussed a number of proposals to deliver some sort of civil, political and economic assistance to Albania.</p>
<p>The proposals included the option of setting up a bridgehead to allow aid to enter ports and the idea of sending police advisers.</p>
</text>
